es pediatric orthopedic market, as well as pediatric orthopedic surgeons and caregivers. OrthoPediatrics Corp. was founded in 2006 and is headquartered in Warsaw, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David R. Bailey | President, CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $886,281 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 602 people. Revenue per employee of $393K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 23%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["OrthoPediatrics Corp. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $845M market cap on $236M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +25% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 75% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $16M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -6.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 30% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 5147% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":51.46942202131095},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $46.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Orthopediatrics Corp. (KIDS) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/11/How_Orthopediatrics_Corp._KIDS_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_110226061401_1793618041.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793618041.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"OrthoPediatrics (KIDS) Q3 Results Spotlight Margin Rebuild After Record Revenue","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-kids/orthopediatrics/news/orthopediatrics-kids-q3-results-spotlight-margin-rebuild-aft","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793402208.514,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.929